title: Monastery Grounds
---
== start
The monastery grounds are quiet and peaceful, surrounded by ancient stone walls and fragrant gardens. A monk in simple robes approaches you with a serene expression.

Monk: "Welcome, traveler, to our humble monastery. In these times of war and strife, we offer sanctuary to those seeking peace and reflection. What brings you to our sacred grounds?"

-> I seek wisdom and guidance.
    Monk: "Wisdom comes not from words alone, but from the quiet contemplation of one's actions. Remember that every choice carries consequences, and mercy often outweighs vengeance."
    <<stop>>

-> I am just passing through.
    Monk: "May your journey bring you safely to your destination. Take this blessing with you: 'Peace be upon you and all you meet.'"
    <<stop>>

-> I need supplies or aid.
    Monk: "We have little to spare, but we can offer you some bread and water for your travels. May it sustain you on your path."
    <<addItem bread, 1>>
    <<stop>>

-> I wish to negotiate sparing your monastery from raids.
    Monk: "You speak of mercy in times of war? Our gardens feed the hungry, and our cellars store the fruits of our labor. What terms do you propose?"
    
    -> I promise to spare your gardens and cellars.
        Monk: "A solemn vow. We accept your word, warrior. May it weigh heavily on your conscience if broken."
        <<addFlag spared_monastery, 1>>
        <<stop>>
    
    -> I cannot make such promises.
        Monk: "Then go with God, but know that mercy is the highest virtue."
        <<stop>>

===
